# image-decoders.plan — the `image.Decode` registry wiring and the two gates that decide which
# uploads this server answers, 2026-09-20. See MIGRATION.md "The remaining image decoders".
#
# `pkg` lines run goimage's own tests (MUTATE_PACKAGE=goimage, no stack); `api` lines run
# parity::image_uploads against the Go server on the stack.
#
# Two kinds of decision are under test here and they fail in opposite directions. A registry arm
# that names the wrong decoder or the wrong format string produces a WRONG ANSWER. A gate that
# forwards the wrong set produces a wrong *hand-over*: too few and the server answers something it
# cannot reproduce, too many and it hands Go work it could have done — the second is invisible to
# every test that only compares served answers, which is why
# `the_undecoded_formats_still_forward` exists and why it asserts Go's measurements too.
#
# `uploads-gate-forgets-unknown` was dropped after 2026-09-20: dropping `| None` from the old
# match left it non-exhaustive, so the line was a HARNESS FAULT rather than a verdict. The gate is
# now a guarded arm and the three lines below mutate the guard instead.
registry-gif-to-bmp	crates/goimage/src/format.rs	Some("gif") => crate::gif::decode(data)\n            .map(|m| (m, "gif"))	Some("gif") => crate::bmp::decode(data)\n            .map(|m| (m, "gif"))	pkg	format::
